  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1243 AM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nLittle change is expected through the forecast period as mid-level \nhigh pressure expands westward across Texas early this week before \ngradually reestablishing over the Four Corners region around \nmidweek. South Texas will remain beneath the influence of the ridge \nthroughout the period, maintaining hot and generally rain-free \nconditions. Afternoon temperatures will continue to range from the \n90s across the Coastal Bend to the Coastal Plains and around 105 \ndegrees across portions of the Rio Grande Plains, with peak heat \nindices around 110 degrees at times. This will maintain a moderate \nto major risk of heat-related impacts across much of South Texas \nthrough the week.\n\nDespite the gradual westward shift of the aforementioned high, \nsufficient ridging and subsidence are expected to persist across the \nregion through next weekend, keeping meaningful rain chances out of \nthe forecast. Overall, expect little day-to-day change with \ncontinued above-normal temperatures, mostly clear to partly cloudy \nskies, and south to southeasterly flow.",
